A presentation without a paper published in a convention/conference/symposium/workshop. THis includes abstract only publications. The next example show how they are cited. The first letter of all main words in the title must be capitalized. Use a three-letter abbreviation for the month, such as Sep. instead of Sept. 
@conference{a_conference_presentation,
  author = {Areti Andreopoulou AND Brian F. G. Katz},
  booktitle = {Meeting Acoust. Soc. Am.},
  title = {Identifying a Perceptually Relevant Estimation Method of the Inter-Aural Time Delay},
  year = {2017},
  month={May},
  address = {Boston, MA}
}


For conference papers published in printed or online proceedings, “in Proc.” will be produced automatically in front of the conference name. Please abbreviate the conference name. The conference acronym may optionally be shown in parentheses, but do not duplicate the year. The page numbers (if available) and conference address (city, county/state) may also be shown. The year and month of publishing and the DOI code must be included (if available), like in this example:
@inproceedings{a_nonAESconference_paper,
  author={Choi, Keunwoo and Fazekas, György and Sandler, Mark and Cho, Kyunghyun},
  title={Convolutional Recurrent Neural Networks for Music Classification}, 
  booktitle={Int. Conf. Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)}, 
  year={2017},
  month={Mar.},
  address={New Orleans, LA},
  pages={2392-2396},
  doi={10.1109/ICASSP.2017.7952585}}

